1	function [MRSCont] = OspreyProcess(MRSCont)
2	%% [MRSCont] = OspreyProcess(MRSCont)
3	%   This function pre-processes MRS data from all major vendors.
4	%   Data is read from the provided input filenames. It is shaped,
5	%   preprocessed, aligned, etc. according to the type of sequence
6	%   (un-edited data, MEGA-edited (ON/OFF), HERMES/HERCULES (A/B/C/D),
7	%   etc.).
8	%
9	%   USAGE:
10	%       MRSCont = OspreyProcess(MRSCont);
11	%
12	%   INPUTS:
13	%       MRSCont     = Osprey MRS data container.
14	%
15	%   OUTPUTS:
16	%       MRSCont     = Osprey MRS data container.
17	%
18	%   AUTHOR:
19	%       Dr. Georg Oeltzschner (Johns Hopkins University, 2019-02-19)
20	%       goeltzs1@jhmi.edu
21	%
22	%   CREDITS:
23	%       This code is based on numerous functions from the FID-A toolbox by
24	%       Dr. Jamie Near (McGill University)
25	%       https://github.com/CIC-methods/FID-A
26	%       Simpson et al., Magn Reson Med 77:23-33 (2017)
27	%
28	%   HISTORY:
29	%       2019-02-19: First version of the code.
30	
31	outputFolder = MRSCont.outputFolder;
